  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If masses of all the molecules of a gas are halved and their speeds are doubled, then the ratio of initial and final pressures is</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>mnv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math> ...(i)<br /><br />and also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8242;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac></math> ...(ii)<br /><br />Dividing Eq.(ii) by Eq. (i), we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8242;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8242;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />The ratio of initial and final pressures is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>."
  }
